DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 2 Advance Concept.

Bash Scripting – Real-World Use Cases (0–2 Years Experience)

Knowing syntax is good.
But real DevOps engineers are hired for automation.

Interviewers often ask:
👉 “What scripts have you written in real life?”

📌 Tool 2 Advance Concept Focus: Practical Bash Scripting Interview Questions

• How do you write a script to check disk usage and send alerts?
• Script to find files older than X days and delete them
• How do you automate log cleanup in Linux?
• Script to monitor CPU and memory usage
• How do you schedule scripts using cron?
• Difference between cron and systemd timers
• How do you write a backup script in bash?
• Script to take application backups with timestamp
• How do you handle errors in bash scripts?
• What is trap in bash?
• How do you debug a bash script?
• Difference between set -e, set -u, and set -o pipefail
• How do you pass arguments to a script?
• How do you log script output to a file?
• How do you write a menu-driven bash script?
• How do you check if a service is running using bash?
• Script to restart a service if it is down
• How do you run a script at system startup?
• How do you secure sensitive data in scripts?
• Real production issue solved using bash scripting

 Interview Tip:
Even a simple statement like:
 “I automated log cleanup and disk monitoring using bash + cron”
can make your profile stand out immediately.
